CloudBurrow patch 1 of 1 to GoogleSQL 2026.7.2 (google/googlesql, tag
2026.7.2, Apache-2.0), as the Cloud Spanner emulator v1.5.58 builds it.
It is applied after the emulator's own build/bazel/googlesql.patch: the
emulator patch 0001 copies it to build/bazel/cloudburrow_googlesql.patch and
lists it in MODULE.bazel's archive_override for googlesql.

Upstream files: googlesql/reference_impl/algebrizer_graph.cc and
googlesql/analyzer/function_signature_matcher.cc.

Why (cloudburrow/cloudburrow#2029):

1. algebrizer_graph.cc, AlgebrizeGraphTableScan: the emulator runs queries
   on GoogleSQL's reference evaluator with scramble_undefined_orderings set
   (backend/query/query_engine.cc), so any relation not marked ordered is
   reordered by ReorderingTupleIterator (odd rows first, then even rows: for
   three rows, the first two swap). GoogleSQL's resolver never sets
   is_ordered on a ResolvedGraphTableScan or on the ResolvedGraphLinearScans
   it wraps, so the projection over a GQL query's final
   `RETURN ... ORDER BY` was marked unordered and its rows came back
   scrambled. Spanner returns them in the ORDER BY's order. The algebrizer
   now reads the order from the last scan of the innermost linear scan (the
   ResolvedOrderByScan, or the ResolvedLimitOffsetScan over it). SQL's ORDER
   BY was never affected: its ResolvedProjectScan and OrderByScan carry
   is_ordered.

2. function_signature_matcher.cc: a graph element was refused for any ANY
   argument unless FEATURE_SQL_GRAPH_EXPOSE_GRAPH_ELEMENT was on, so
   `LET path_length = COUNT(t)` over a group variable (Google's documented
   ANY SHORTEST example, graph-patterns page) failed with "No matching
   signature for aggregate function COUNT". Spanner documents that "Graph
   elements can be used in GQL predicates, functions and subqueries within
   GQL". With FEATURE_SQL_GRAPH on, graph elements exist only inside a graph
   query (RETURN and COLUMNS still refuse a graph-typed column without
   EXPOSE_GRAPH_ELEMENT), so the matcher now takes them there.

diff --git a/googlesql/analyzer/function_signature_matcher.cc b/googlesql/analyzer/function_signature_matcher.cc
index 3495907..4776337 100644
--- a/googlesql/analyzer/function_signature_matcher.cc
+++ b/googlesql/analyzer/function_signature_matcher.cc
@@ -1573,8 +1573,13 @@ absl::StatusOr<bool> FunctionSignatureMatcher::
       if (
           // Disallow graph types when the signature does not *explicitly* take
           // graph element types: even if the signature type is ANY.
+          // Graph elements only exist inside a graph query when
+          // FEATURE_SQL_GRAPH_EXPOSE_GRAPH_ELEMENT is off (the RETURN and
+          // COLUMNS checks keep them from leaving it), and GQL takes them
+          // in any function there, e.g. COUNT(e) of a group variable.
           (!language_.LanguageFeatureEnabled(
                FEATURE_SQL_GRAPH_EXPOSE_GRAPH_ELEMENT) &&
+           !language_.LanguageFeatureEnabled(FEATURE_SQL_GRAPH) &&
            input_type != nullptr && input_type->IsGraphElement()) ||
           // Disallow measure types for templated arguments except
           // ARG_KIND_EXPR_MEASURE_ANY_1.
diff --git a/googlesql/reference_impl/algebrizer_graph.cc b/googlesql/reference_impl/algebrizer_graph.cc
index fdbf7db..2d9b8f8 100644
--- a/googlesql/reference_impl/algebrizer_graph.cc
+++ b/googlesql/reference_impl/algebrizer_graph.cc
@@ -383,6 +383,19 @@ TryGetNodeReferencesFromEdgeReferences(
 
   return result;
 }
+// Whether a GQL query's result is ordered: the resolver leaves is_ordered
+// unset on the ResolvedGraphTableScan and on the ResolvedGraphLinearScans it
+// wraps, so the order of a final `RETURN ... ORDER BY` (a ResolvedOrderByScan,
+// or a ResolvedLimitOffsetScan over one) is read from the last scan of the
+// innermost linear scan, which is the scan whose rows the query returns.
+bool GqlFinalScanIsOrdered(const ResolvedScan* scan) {
+  while (scan != nullptr && scan->Is<ResolvedGraphLinearScan>()) {
+    const auto* linear = scan->GetAs<ResolvedGraphLinearScan>();
+    if (linear->scan_list().empty()) return false;
+    scan = linear->scan_list().back().get();
+  }
+  return scan != nullptr && scan->is_ordered();
+}
 }  // namespace
 
 absl::StatusOr<std::unique_ptr<RelationalOp>>
@@ -398,7 +411,9 @@ Algebrizer::AlgebrizeGraphTableScan(
   // and not embed the expressions in it.
   return AlgebrizeProjectScanInternal(
       graph_table_scan->column_list(), graph_table_scan->shape_expr_list(),
-      graph_table_scan->input_scan(), graph_table_scan->is_ordered(),
+      graph_table_scan->input_scan(),
+      graph_table_scan->is_ordered() ||
+          GqlFinalScanIsOrdered(graph_table_scan->input_scan()),
       active_conjuncts);
 }
 
